The National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC) has confirmed that 48 persons have died in Ondo State after consuming a contaminated herbal mixture.

Director-General of NAFDAC said laboratory tests revealed methanol concentrations over 400% above safe limits.

> "This is one of the most tragic cases of fake drug poisoning we have seen in recent years."

The agency has sealed three production sites in Akure and Owo local government areas.
